Let $p$ be the cost of a pencil and $q$ be the cost of a pen. We are given the following equations:
\begin{align*}
5p + q &= 2.50 \quad \text{(1)} \\
p + 2q &= 1.85 \quad \text{(2)}
\end{align*}
To solve for $p$ and $q$, we can multiply equation (1) by $2$ and then subtract equation (2):
\begin{align*}
10p + 2q &= 5.00 \\
p + 2q &= 1.85 \\
\hline
9p &= 3.15
\end{align*}
Dividing both sides by $9$, we find that $p = 0.35$. Substituting this value back into equation (2), we find that $q = 0.70$. Therefore, the cost of two pencils and one pen is $2p + q = 2(0.35) + 0.70 = \boxed{1.40}$. The answer is: 1.40
